{% extends "page/checkout/thankyou.html.twig" %}

{#
    2026-09-01 — a payment still settling is not an error.

    A PSP that returns the customer while the payment is still open has one way
    to say so between two requests: UtilsView::addErrorToDisplay(). The shop
    paints everything in that channel as a dismissible red alert above the whole
    page, so the customer's order went through and the first thing they saw was
    red — directly above the words "Thank you".

    payment-base's ThankYouController extension takes those messages out of the
    stash while the page renders, which is what removes the banner; here they
    come back as what they always were, inside the thank-you text.

    First, deliberately: "your payment is being processed" changes how the rest
    of the block should be read, so it cannot come after it.

    `raw` matches how core renders the same messages in message/errors.html.twig
    — they are shop and module lang strings, and some carry markup.
#}
{% block checkout_thankyou_info %}
    {% for notice in oView.getPaymentNotices() %}
        <div class="alert alert-info" id="paymentNotice" role="status">{{ notice|raw }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
    {{ parent() }}
{% endblock %}
